import AxQM.Postulates.API.FourGateNamedTowerDensity

/-!
# `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` with measurement are universal
(N&C Exercise 4.43)

The two ingredients of Exercise 4.43's four-gate claim are in
`AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateNamedTowerDensity.lean`:

* `exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_namedFourGateTowerGates` — **the density core.** For
  `cos θ = 3/5`, the four-gate tower model `namedFourGateTowerGates n θ` — generated by the four
  named gates `hadamardGate, sGate, cnotGate, toffoliGate` **and** the base rotation `rotZGate θ`
  as a generator — is dense up to a global phase. On its own it carries `rotZGate θ` as a **free**
  unitary generator, so it is not the four-gate claim.
* `rzThreeFifthsMeasurement_success_realizes_rotZ` — **the four-gate measurement realisation.** The
  Figure-4.17 circuit `rzThreeFifthsCircuit` (`H, S, Toffoli` on two ancillas + target) followed by
  the two-ancilla measurement `rzTwoAncillaMeasurement`, on the success outcome `(0, 0)`
  (probability `‖c‖² = 5/8`), applies `R_z(rzThreeFifthsAngle)` to the target.

This file combines them: it *removes* the free `rotZGate θ` generator, replacing it by a
**measurement-realised generator set**, so that Exercise 4.43's conclusion is stated without
positing the irrational rotation as a fifth gate.

## Contents

* `IsFourGateMeasurementRealised G` — **the measurement-realisation predicate.** A single-qubit
  gate `G : Evolution qubit` is *realised by the four-gate measurement gadget* when the Figure-4.17
  circuit `rzThreeFifthsCircuit`, post-selected on the success outcome `(0, 0)` of the two-ancilla
  measurement `rzTwoAncillaMeasurement`, applies `G` to the target: its first conjunct is the
  circuit + measurement's success action (`… = rzThreeFifthsAmp 0 0 t • |0,0,t⟩`), and its second
  conjunct pins `G` to that success amplitude (`rzThreeFifthsAmp 0 0 t • |t⟩ = c • G.op |t⟩`,
  `‖c‖² = 5/8`) — so `G.op` is determined
  on the computational basis up to the global scalar `c`, i.e. `G = R_z(θ)` up to an (unobservable)
  global phase. It is exactly the conclusion of `rzThreeFifthsMeasurement_success_realizes_rotZ`
  with the concrete `rotZGate rzThreeFifthsAngle` abstracted to a variable `G`.
* `isFourGateMeasurementRealised_rotZGate_rzThreeFifthsAngle` — the base rotation is realised:
  `IsFourGateMeasurementRealised (rotZGate rzThreeFifthsAngle)`, immediately from the
  realisation. This is the key link: the only rotation the four *unitary* gates cannot
  themselves generate is supplied by their **measurement**.
* `fourGateMeasurementReachable n` — **the four-gate + measurement tower model.** The same submonoid
  as `namedFourGateTowerGates n`, but with the free rotation generator `rotZGate θ` **replaced** by
  the measurement-realised set `{G | IsFourGateMeasurementRealised G}`: it is generated by the
  tower-wire placements of the four named *unitary* gates `hadamardGate, sGate` (with `cnotGate,
  toffoliGate` entering through the named reversible gates `namedMcNotGate`) together with the
  tower-wire placements of *every gate the four-gate measurement gadget realises*. No `rotZGate`
  appears as a free generator — every rotation in the model is present because it is
  measurement-realised.
* `namedFourGateTowerGates_rzThreeFifthsAngle_le_fourGateMeasurementReachable` — the density core's
  model sits inside the measurement model: `namedFourGateTowerGates n rzThreeFifthsAngle ≤
  fourGateMeasurementReachable n`, by `Submonoid.closure_mono` — the `hadamardGate, sGate` and
  reversible generators are shared, and the rotation generator `rotZGate rzThreeFifthsAngle` lies in
  the measurement-realised set (`isFourGateMeasurementRealised_rotZGate_rzThreeFifthsAngle`).
* `hsCnotToffoli_measurement_universal` — **the main theorem.** For any tower evolution
  `T : Evolution (qtower n qubit)`, some global phase `e^{iα}` makes `e^{iα} • T.op` lie in the
  closure of the operator image of `fourGateMeasurementReachable n`: the circuits built from the
  four gates `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` **together with the measurement-realised rotation** are dense in
  the unitaries up to a global phase. Immediate from the density core at `θ := rzThreeFifthsAngle`
  (`rzThreeFifthsAngle_cos`) and the containment, by `closure_mono`.

Because the model's rotation generators are constrained (by `IsFourGateMeasurementRealised`, which
names `rzThreeFifthsCircuit` and `rzTwoAncillaMeasurement`) to be gates the four-gate measurement
circuit realises — rather than an unconstrained `rotZGate θ` — the statement reads as Exercise
4.43 intends: `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` **with measurement** (Exercises 4.41/4.42) are universal for
quantum computation. The statement of Exercise 4.43 is in `AxQM/NC/Ch4/Exercise4_43.lean`.
-/

namespace AxQM

noncomputable section

/-- **A single-qubit gate realised by the four-gate measurement gadget** (N&C Exercise 4.41). `G`
is *realised* when the Figure-4.17 circuit `rzThreeFifthsCircuit` (`H, S, Toffoli` on two ancillas +
target), followed by the two-ancilla measurement `rzTwoAncillaMeasurement` post-selected on the
success outcome `(0, 0)`, applies `G` to the target:

* the success (Kraus) operator sends the circuit output on `|0, 0, t⟩` to
  `rzThreeFifthsAmp 0 0 t • |0, 0, t⟩` (the circuit + measurement's success action), and
* that amplitude equals `c • G.op` on the target for a scalar `c` with `‖c‖² = 5/8` (the
  input-independent success probability), which pins `G.op` on the computational basis up to the
  global scalar `c` — so `G` is `R_z(rzThreeFifthsAngle)` up to a global phase.

This is precisely `rzThreeFifthsMeasurement_success_realizes_rotZ` with the concrete
`rotZGate rzThreeFifthsAngle` abstracted to the variable `G`; naming `rzThreeFifthsCircuit` and the
measurement `rzTwoAncillaMeasurement`, it is what a generator's being "supplied by the
four gates + measurement" means, replacing the free `rotZGate θ` generator of the density core. -/
def IsFourGateMeasurementRealised (G : Evolution qubit) : Prop :=
  (∀ t : Fin 2,
      (rzTwoAncillaMeasurement.op (0, 0))
          (rzThreeFifthsCircuit.evolvePure
            ((qubitBasis 0).tmul ((qubitBasis 0).tmul (qubitBasis t)))).vec
        = rzThreeFifthsAmp 0 0 t •
            ((qubitBasis 0).tmul ((qubitBasis 0).tmul (qubitBasis t))).vec) ∧
    ∃ c : ℂ, ‖c‖ ^ 2 = 5 / 8 ∧ ∀ t : Fin 2,
      rzThreeFifthsAmp 0 0 t • (qubitBasis t).vec
        = c • G.op (qubitBasis t).vec

/-- **The base rotation is realised by the four gates + measurement.**
`IsFourGateMeasurementRealised (rotZGate rzThreeFifthsAngle)` — the irrational rotation `R_z(θ)`
(`cos θ = 3/5`), the sole gate the four *unitary* gates cannot generate, is supplied by their
measurement (Exercise 4.41). Immediate from the realisation
`rzThreeFifthsMeasurement_success_realizes_rotZ`. -/
theorem isFourGateMeasurementRealised_rotZGate_rzThreeFifthsAngle :
    IsFourGateMeasurementRealised (rotZGate rzThreeFifthsAngle) :=
  rzThreeFifthsMeasurement_success_realizes_rotZ

/-- **The four-gate + measurement tower model.** The submonoid of `Evolution (qtower n qubit)`
generated by

* the single-tower-wire placements `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i g` of the named *unitary* gates
  `g ∈ {hadamardGate, sGate}` together with *every* measurement-realised gate
  `g ∈ {G | IsFourGateMeasurementRealised G}`, over every wire `i`, and
* the shared named reversible tower generators `namedReversibleTowerGenerators n`
  (`Core/FourGateNamedTower`) — the named gates `namedMcNotGate k` (`k ≤ 2` — `NOT = H·S²·H`,
  `cnotGate`, `toffoliGate`) placed on a wire set and transported onto the tower — *the very same*
  reversible half `namedFourGateTowerGates` uses.

This is `namedFourGateTowerGates n θ` with the free rotation generator `rotZGate θ` **replaced** by
the measurement-realised set (the reversible half is literally shared): no `rotZGate` is posited as
a generator; every rotation in the model is present only because the four-gate measurement gadget
realises it. Its unitary generators are the four named gates `hadamardGate, sGate, cnotGate,
toffoliGate`. -/
def fourGateMeasurementReachable (n : ℕ) :
    Submonoid (Evolution (qtower n qubit)) :=
  Submonoid.closure
    ((⋃ i : Fin (n + 1),
        Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i ''
          (insert hadamardGate (insert sGate {G | IsFourGateMeasurementRealised G}))) ∪
      namedReversibleTowerGenerators n)

/-- **The density core's model sits inside the four-gate + measurement model.**
`namedFourGateTowerGates n rzThreeFifthsAngle ≤ fourGateMeasurementReachable n`.

By `Submonoid.closure_mono` it suffices that the generating set of the named four-gate submonoid is
contained in that of the measurement model: the reversible-generator half is *literally shared* (the
common `namedReversibleTowerGenerators n`, so its inclusion is `subset_refl`), and on the rotation
half `{hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate rzThreeFifthsAngle} ⊆
insert hadamardGate (insert sGate {G | IsFourGateMeasurementRealised G})` because `hadamardGate` and
`sGate` are shared and the base rotation `rotZGate rzThreeFifthsAngle` is measurement-realised
(`isFourGateMeasurementRealised_rotZGate_rzThreeFifthsAngle`). -/
theorem namedFourGateTowerGates_rzThreeFifthsAngle_le_fourGateMeasurementReachable (n : ℕ) :
    namedFourGateTowerGates n rzThreeFifthsAngle ≤ fourGateMeasurementReachable n := by
  apply Submonoid.closure_mono
  refine Set.union_subset_union ?_ (subset_refl (namedReversibleTowerGenerators n))
  refine Set.iUnion_mono fun i => Set.image_mono ?_
  exact Set.insert_subset_insert (Set.insert_subset_insert
    (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr isFourGateMeasurementRealised_rotZGate_rzThreeFifthsAngle))

/-- **`H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` with measurement are universal for quantum computation** (N&C Exercise
4.43). For *any* tower evolution `T : Evolution (qtower n qubit)`, some global phase `e^{iα}` makes

  `e^{iα} • T.op ∈ closure ((·.op) '' fourGateMeasurementReachable n)`,

so every unitary on the `(n+1)`-qubit control tower is, up to an (unobservable) global phase, a
limit of the operators of circuits drawn from the four-gate + measurement model
`fourGateMeasurementReachable n` — the circuits built from `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` together with the
measurement-realised rotation `R_z(θ)`.

Unlike the density core `exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_namedFourGateTowerGates`, the rotation
generator here is **not** a freely-posited `rotZGate θ` but any gate the four-gate measurement
gadget realises (`IsFourGateMeasurementRealised`, naming `rzThreeFifthsCircuit` and
`rzTwoAncillaMeasurement` — Exercises 4.41/4.42); the irrational rotation the four *unitary* gates
cannot generate is *derived* from their measurement, not assumed. This is Exercise 4.43's
universality conclusion.

Immediate from the density core at `θ := rzThreeFifthsAngle` (`rzThreeFifthsAngle_cos`) and the
containment `namedFourGateTowerGates_rzThreeFifthsAngle_le_fourGateMeasurementReachable`, by
`closure_mono` (`SetLike.coe_subset_coe` + `Set.image_mono`). -/
theorem hsCnotToffoli_measurement_universal {n : ℕ} (T : Evolution (qtower n qubit)) :
    ∃ α : ℝ, Complex.exp ((α : ℂ) * Complex.I) • T.op ∈
      closure ((fun E : Evolution (qtower n qubit) => E.op) ''
        (fourGateMeasurementReachable n : Set (Evolution (qtower n qubit)))) := by
  obtain ⟨α, hα⟩ :=
    exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_namedFourGateTowerGates rzThreeFifthsAngle_cos T
  exact ⟨α, closure_mono (Set.image_mono (SetLike.coe_subset_coe.2
    (namedFourGateTowerGates_rzThreeFifthsAngle_le_fourGateMeasurementReachable n))) hα⟩

end

